      },
      {
        "class": "FLAW-0013",
        "dials": {
          "count": 7,
          "inserted": "Recall the definition of parity: a natural number $n$ is even when $2 \\mid n$, that is, when $n \\bmod 2 = 0$, and odd otherwise, that is, when $n \\bmod 2 = 1$; every natural number is one or the other.",
          "kind": "restated-definition",
