        "dials": {
          "count": 7,
          "inserted": "Here is a second derivation of the same fact: if $p$ were odd, say $p = 2m + 1$, then $p^2 = 4m^2 + 4m + 1 = 2(2m^2 + 2m) + 1$ would be odd, so $2 \\nmid p^2$; therefore $2 \\mid p^2$ forces $p$ to be even.",
